				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				690,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add short mode to dev logging for reduced output verbosity\n\nShort mode (`LAND_DEV_LOG=short`) compresses Rust module targets (D::Binary::Main::Entry → Entry), aliases the verbose app-data path (~Library/Application Support/land.editor.*mountain*) to $APP, and deduplicates consecutive identical messages with an (xN) suffix.\n\nThis builds on the recent 38-tag expansion by reducing visual noise during local development. Changes: CompressTarget() function in LoggingPlugin, APP_DATA_PREFIX detection + AliasPath() in DevLog, DEDUP state machine for deduplication, and conditional StorageProvider logging that uses dev_log! instead of info! in short mode.",
			"SHA": "2348f18ad204cb92e3c2ae6d6263585ce3c0ac84"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-10T21:27:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				690,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add 38 granular dev logging tags across IPC and bootstrap\n\nExpand DevLog system from 8 tags to 38 granular tags covering all service areas: terminal, extensions, search, themes, window, nativehost, clipboard, commands, model, output, notification, progress, quickinput, workingcopy, workspaces, keybinding, label, history, decorations, textfile, update, encryption, menubar, url, grpc, cocoon, bootstrap, preload.\n\nAdd dev_log!() calls to every IPC command handler in WindServiceHandlers with matching category tags. Fix session timestamp to be generated once per process lifetime so getEnvironmentPaths returns consistent logsPath. Add vscode-file://vscode-app to CSP for VS Code file protocol.\n\nImprove CocoonManagement: resolve bootstrap script from Tauri resources (prod) or relative to executable (dev), preserve PATH/HOME env vars, add orphan detection for parent process, and delegate to compiled entry point or stub keep-alive.\n\nThis enables fine-grained development debugging: LAND_DEV_LOG=terminal,exthost ./Mountain or browser console __LAND_DEV_LOG.",
			"SHA": "d92cd0a4d1d9d189a950d2b5a3cddb5b6fcf8ad0"
		}
	],
